Z||000000||Uaana||05-23-2000||06:42 PM||||Just a couple of things before I forget.<BR>1. for the people who were looking for leather mirror covers, (take them off a corvette, same thing)<BR>2 for people restoring wheels, pyroil carb cleaner does a great job of removing clearcoat and alot of the stains on the wheels.<BR>thanks for the space.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000001||Raydar||05-23-2000||08:31 PM||||Uaana,<P>Good info. <P>I have also heard that the Firebird mirrors are the same. Dunno about leather covers.<P>Will the carb cleaner strip paint? Like the stuff on the GT wheels?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||05-24-2000||12:09 AM||||Not too sure about the paint yet. I've been playing around with a pair of "tech" wheels, and don't really want to strip the paint yet and I think the paint on there is a more durable enamel. If you were to want to remove that I would suggest one of the citrus strippers that you can paint on and wash off and is "eco" friendly.<BR>Ok had to get in on that little rant in my own way.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Oreif||05-24-2000||01:25 AM||||I have a set of 15" GT wheels I am refinishing (yes I restarted) I tried a few different paint strippers and the one that worked the best was Permatex spray on gasket remover. It took 1/2 the time as the paint stripper stuff! You can also buy a bottle with a little brush of the same stuff so you can only strip what you want. (I am doing the entire wheel so I bought the spray)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Flash Box||05-24-2000||11:54 AM||||I know the paint on wheels is a little different, but I got some Carb cleaner on my Camaro valve covers and it blistered the paint up real fast. I am going to powder coat them now. ||||reg||2
Z||000005||Raydar||05-24-2000||04:58 PM||||Thanks, guys.<BR>When I stripped my wheels, I used that really nasty, caustic stripper that they sell at Home Depot. Just hosed it off, into the yard. Was NOT a lot of fun.||||reg||1
